{
  "id": "banat_taragot_music",
  "name": "Muzică bănățeană (Banat taragot and dance music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Regional folk and dance music of the Romanian Banat around Timișoara, in which the taragot, a keyed single-reed woodwind brought from Hungary, where it is called tárogató, by Banat lăutari in the twentieth century, became a leading melody instrument alongside violin, clarinet, saxophone, accordion and double bass. It accompanies Banat dances such as the brâu, often in a limping seven-beat metre, and the swift de doi couple dance, as well as slow songs and doinas, and its taragot soloists and singers were recorded by Electrecord and Radio Timișoara. The tárogató card stands in for the taragot.",
  "recipe": "classic Eastern European early-1940s muzică bănățeană, wedding, European branch. single lead single track no stacking. tarogato, fiddle, saxophone, accordion, norway spruce European alpine European maple sycamore maple kolstein double bass. hardwood living. large-diaphragm condenser, German V72 tube pre, German tube console, vari-mu, passive program EQ. tape 15ips plate reverb.",
